The paper, “Re(Visiting) Large Language Models in Finance” by Eghbal Rahimikia and Felix Drinkall, evaluates the effectiveness of specialized large language models (LLMs) designed for accounting and finance tasks. The authors introduce FinText, a series of domain-specific LLMs that are significantly smaller than state-of-the-art general-purpose models like LLaMA but outperform them in predicting stock returns.

